// Seven equal bars on a 7:10 field; the third and fifth are a gradient across the fly.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Demifluid flag"
  designer "pbjkid (Tumblr)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2015-02-18"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20150520162452/http://pride-flags-for-us.tumblr.com/post/111369359919/demigenderfluid-or-demifluid-gender-changes"
  source "https://64.media.tumblr.com/a3bb591216df556a7e1bd0dbcd1913a0/tumblr_njyqtc8knr1u5udwoo1_500.png"
  note "Defining source: the submission 'demigenderfluid or demifluid - gender changes between demigenders' on pride-flags-for-us, posted 18 February 2015 (read at the snapshot above). Its notes say pbjkid submitted it; that blog was later deactivated. The post gives no meanings, hex or proportion. It has two images: this one, whose pink, yellow and blue bars blend into each other, and a second with the three colors in separate blocks, which is not written."
  note "Construction and colors are read from the first image (477 by 334 PNG, read). It is the demigender pattern: grey #7f7f7f, light grey #c3c3c3, a gradient, white #ffffff, the gradient again, light grey, grey. The gradient runs #ffa9d0 at the hoist, #fff1a6 at the middle and #a0d9fd at the fly, and is a straight blend between them within 2 units per channel. This is my sampling, not hex the designer gave. The bars are 53, 47, 44, 46, 46, 46 and 52 pixels, which I take as drawing error; they are equal here."
  note "The 7:10 proportion is rounded from the image (1.43), the same base as Salem's demigirl and demiboy proposals; Pride-Flags draws 3:5."
}
palette {
  grey "#7f7f7f"
  light-grey "#c3c3c3"
  white "#ffffff"
  pink "#ffa9d0"
  yellow "#fff1a6"
  blue "#a0d9fd"
  fluid gradient pink yellow blue
}
proportion hoist=7 fly=10

bars grey light-grey fluid white fluid light-grey grey
